# Time stepping parameters
 &PARM03
#2026-10-01 RESTART FROM SCRATCH, SEGMENT 1 OF A NEW CHAIN. Was nIter0=751680
#(segment 2 of the previous chain, job 25210810, killed by signal 15 at 02:24
#on 09-30 and never logged).
#
#WHY THE WHOLE CHAIN IS VOID, not resumable. That chain's dv output was
#extracted through the masks in run/dv/ at the time, which were built on the
#stitched grid's SQUARE perimeter. pan_AO is a polar stereographic DISC: the
#model array's square edge is not the open boundary (174 of 6720 cells wet,
#east edge 0 wet). The masks were regenerated along the rim on 09-30 by
#gen_dvmasks_disc.py (job 25215198) and are a DIFFERENT GEOMETRY with
#DIFFERENT POINT COUNTS -- west 0->736, east 265->141, south 324->685,
#north 358->256. There are no common bytes between old and new output, so
#nothing can be reused and nothing can be stitched across the change. The 249
#old files are archived in run/dv_SQUARE_BOUNDARY_defective/ as history only;
#do not diff against them (same trap as dv_hourly_partial_killed_25187803).
#
#The west boundary is also BACK in data.diagnostics_vec (20 entries, not 15)
#and DIAGNOSTICS_VEC_SIZE.h nVEC_mask is 20 to match, which REQUIRED A
#REBUILD. A restart at the old nIter0 with the new 20-mask config would be the
#worst of both worlds: diagnostics_vec_init_fixed.F:76-77 resets
#vec_time_levels to (1, nIter0+1) on every startup, and the STATUS='OLD'
#interleaving hazard bites precisely when a segment restarts at the SAME
#nIter0 -- it would write new-geometry records into the old-geometry files.
#Starting from 736344 sidesteps that entirely: run/dv/ is empty of output.
#
#Back to the original pickup, iter 736344 (all 5 filesets present as symlinks
#into v05_latest/darwin3/run, confirmed 2026-10-01).
#
#CHAINING, unchanged and still required: each restart writes its own
#independent file set *_<nIter0+1>.bin with records restarting at 1, named by
#CREATE_FILENAME_VEC from vec_time_levels(.,2). Segments must be stitched, not
#concatenated blindly, and a segment that overruns its successor's pickup
#leaves redone overlap records at its tail to discard. See stage_dv_segments.py.
 nIter0=604872,
#pan_AO FULL 1-YEAR PARENT dv EXTRACTION (Milestone 2 gate closed
#2026-09-22 -- round-2 debug run confirmed record-index/write path
#correct, see DECISIONS.md): restart from the same 2020-01-01 pickup
#Fiji uses (nIter0=736344), run 1 simulated year to 2021-01-01, same
#duration/endtime as fiji's completed fijidv run (job 25148838).
#endtime is ABSOLUTE model myTime (seconds since 1992-01-01, data.cal
#base), NOT a duration: nIter0*deltaT (736344*1200=883,612,800) +
#26352*1200 (31,622,400) = 915,235,200 = iteration 762696.
 endtime=1072958400.,
 forcing_In_AB=.FALSE.,
 momDissip_In_AB=.FALSE.,
#when using the cd scheme:
# epsAB_CD = 0.25,
# tauCD=172800.0,
 deltaTmom   =1200.,
 deltaTtracer=1200.,
 deltaTfreesurf=1200.,
 deltaTClock =1200.,
#when using ab2:
# abEps = 0.1,
#when using ab3:
 doAB_onGtGs=.FALSE.,
 alph_AB=0.5,
 beta_AB=0.281105,
#
#2026-09-28: pChkptFreq cut 31536000.0 (365d) -> 2592000.0 (30d = 2160
#iterations at deltaT=1200). The hourly-cadence dv extraction is projected
#at ~139h wall (job 25187803 reached only 34.6% in its 48h cap), which
#exceeds the `long` queue's own 120h hard max -- so this run CANNOT finish
#in one submission and must be chained across restarts. At the old 365d
#setting the only pickup boundary fell at the very end of the window, so a
#walltime kill lost all progress (exactly what happened to 25187803).
#At 30d there are ~12 named restart points, capping loss at ~11h wall.
#chkptFreq (rolling ckptA/ckptB) left at 365d on purpose: the permanent
#pickups are now frequent enough to be the restart points, and they carry
#an unambiguous iteration number, which the ckptA/ckptB pair does not.
 pChkptFreq  =2592000.0,
 chkptFreq   =31536000.0,
# taveFreq    =31536000.0,
# dumpFreq    =31536000.0,
 monitorFreq = 43200.0,
# monitorFreq = 6307200.0,
 dumpInitAndLast = .FALSE.,
 pickupStrictlyMatch=.FALSE.,
